import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Documentation — Ofir" description="Get started with Ofir: build the compiler, run a program, and explore the language reference." page="docs">
<main id="main" class="docs-layout shell">
    <aside class="docs-sidebar" aria-label="Documentation sections"><span class="sidebar-title">ON THIS PAGE</span><a href="#overview">Overview</a><a href="#getting-started">Get started</a><a href="#first-program">Your first program</a><a href="#next-steps">Explore further</a><div class="sidebar-divider"></div><span class="sidebar-title">REFERENCE</span><a href="https://github.com/lucasgmagalhaes/ofir/blob/main/docs/spec/README.md">Language specification ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/lucasgmagalhaes/ofir/blob/main/docs/std/README.md">Standard library ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/lucasgmagalhaes/ofir/blob/main/docs/errors/README.md">Error codes ↗</a></aside>
    <div class="docs-main">
      <div class="docs-breadcrumb">DOCS <span>/</span> GETTING STARTED</div>
      <section id="overview" class="docs-hero"><h1>Get to know<br><em>Ofir.</em></h1><p>Everything you need to compile and run your first Ofir program.</p></section>
      <div class="docs-callout"><p>Ofir is under active development. The <a href="https://github.com/lucasgmagalhaes/ofir/blob/main/docs/roadmap.md">roadmap</a> tracks what is implemented and what is planned.</p></div>
      <section id="getting-started" class="docs-section"><div class="docs-section-label">01 / SETUP</div><h2>Get started</h2><p>Clone the repository, then build the stage 0 compiler and runtime. You will need a C11 compiler, <code>make</code>, Python 3, and clang 17 or later.</p><div class="doc-code"><div class="doc-code-head"><span>TERMINAL · MACOS / LINUX</span><button class="copy-button" type="button" data-copy="git clone https://github.com/lucasgmagalhaes/ofir.git&#10;cd ofir&#10;make" aria-label="Copy setup commands">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="prompt">$</span> git clone https://github.com/lucasgmagalhaes/ofir.git
<span class="prompt">$</span> cd ofir
<span class="prompt">$</span> make</code></pre></div><p>On Windows, use Git Bash, clang, and a MinGW-w64 toolchain; run <code>mingw32-make</code> instead of <code>make</code>. See the <a href="https://github.com/lucasgmagalhaes/ofir/blob/main/docs/design/toolchain.md#windows">Windows setup guide</a> for details.</p></section>
      <section id="first-program" class="docs-section"><div class="docs-section-label">02 / HELLO WORLD</div><h2>Your first program</h2><p>Create <code>hello.of</code> with a <code>main</code> function. String interpolation puts the value of <code>name</code> into the greeting.</p><div class="doc-code"><div class="doc-code-head"><span>hello.of</span><button class="copy-button" type="button" data-copy="fn main() &#123;&#10;    const name = &quot;Ofir&quot;&#10;    println(&quot;Hello, &#123;name&#125;!&quot;)&#10;&#125;" aria-label="Copy first program">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="syntax-purple">fn</span> main() &#123;
    <span class="syntax-purple">const</span> name = <span class="syntax-yellow">"Ofir"</span>
    println(<span class="syntax-yellow">"Hello, &#123;name&#125;!"</span>)
&#125;</code></pre></div><p>Run it with the compiler you just built:</p><div class="doc-code"><div class="doc-code-head"><span>TERMINAL</span><button class="copy-button" type="button" data-copy="build/stage0/ofir run hello.of" aria-label="Copy run command">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="prompt">$</span> build/stage0/ofir run hello.of
Hello, Ofir!</code></pre></div></section>
      <section id="next-steps" class="docs-section"><div class="docs-section-label">03 / KEEP GOING</div><h2>Explore further</h2><p>Use the repository's references to learn the language and its tools.</p><div class="docs-links"><a href="https://github.com/lucasgmagalhaes/ofir/blob/main/docs/spec/README.md"><strong>Language specification <span>↗</span></strong><small>Syntax, types, ownership, modules, and more.</small></a><a href="https://github.com/lucasgmagalhaes/ofir/blob/main/docs/std/README.md"><strong>Standard library <span>↗</span></strong><small>Core types, collections, strings, and system APIs.</small></a><a href="https://github.com/lucasgmagalhaes/ofir/blob/main/docs/design/toolchain.md"><strong>Toolchain guide <span>↗</span></strong><small>Compiler commands, formatting, and build process.</small></a><a href="https://github.com/lucasgmagalhaes/ofir/tree/main/examples"><strong>Examples <span>↗</span></strong><small>Small programs you can read and run.</small></a></div></section>
    </div>
    <aside class="docs-toc" aria-label="Page outline"><span class="sidebar-title">IN THIS GUIDE</span><a href="#getting-started">Get started</a><a href="#first-program">Your first program</a><a href="#next-steps">Explore further</a></aside>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
